</style><style>.bcx .ticketing{background:var(--paper);border-top:1px solid var(--ink);border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink)}.bcx .ticketing-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr .9fr;gap:70px;align-items:center}.bcx .ticketing p{margin-bottom:0}.bcx .ticket-actions{display:grid;gap:18px}.bcx .ticket-choice{display:grid;gap:10px}.bcx .ticket-btn{width:100%;border:0;border-radius:0;cursor:pointer}.bcx .ticket-choice>a{font-weight:800;text-align:center}.bcx .ticket-btn:disabled{cursor:wait;opacity:.65}@media(max-width:820px){.bcx .ticketing-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:30px}}</style><main class="bcx campaign" style="--accent:#F47C20" id="main-content"><header class="hero"><div class="hero-copy"><h1>Atlanta Halloween Bar Crawls 2026</h1><p class="lede">The BeltLine Has Costumes Now. Atlanta Has Plans.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="#tickets">Put Me on the BeltLine</a><a class="btn alt" href="#route">See the route</a></div></div><div class="hero-media"><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Atlanta-Bar-Crawl-USA-crowd.webp" alt="Friends gathering at a Bar Crawl USA event in Atlanta" width="1200" height="900" fetchpriority="high"></div></header><div class="facts" aria-label="Event quick facts"><div class="fact"><span>Date</span><strong>Saturday, October 31</strong></div><div class="fact"><span>Published time</span><strong>6 PM to Midnight</strong></div><div class="fact"><span>Neighborhood</span><strong>Atlanta BeltLine Eastside Trail</strong></div></div><section class="ticketing" id="tickets"><div class="wrap ticketing-grid"><div><h2>Tickets without the detour.</h2><p>Choose your event and complete the secure Eventbrite checkout without leaving this page. Use the event details link when you need the latest route or check in update.</p></div><div class="ticket-actions"><div class="ticket-choice"><button class="btn ticket-btn" id="eb-atlanta-halloween-bar-crawls-2026-1" type="button">Buy Atlanta BeltLine tickets</button><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/event/atlanta-beltline-halloween-bar-crawl/">Review event details</a></div></div></div></section><section class="story"><div class="wrap"><h2>BrewDog starts it. The Eastside Trail carries it. Ten named stops give your group enough choices to make a strategy and enough room to ignore it. Midtown joins this page only when its own 2026 details are real.</h2><p>Atlanta does Halloween two ways: trail side energy on the BeltLine and a Midtown edition that will be added here only when its 2026 details are confirmed. The live BeltLine crawl is the decision ready option today, with registration at BrewDog Krog District and a published route across the Eastside Trail.</p><p>This is a walking, choose your own pace night built around the Eastside Trail. Start by checking in at BrewDog Krog District, collect your lanyard and map, then use the official route as your anchor. The strongest plan is to arrive with your group before the registration window gets busy, pick three must visit stops, and leave room for the costume contest back at BrewDog.</p><div class="edition-grid"><article><h3>BeltLine is live</h3><p>October 31 from 6 PM to midnight. Registration starts at BrewDog Krog District.</p><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/event/atlanta-beltline-halloween-bar-crawl/">Choose the BeltLine event</a></article><article><h3>Midtown waits for facts</h3><p>No verified 2026 Midtown Halloween record is public. This page will not make one up.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="value"><div class="wrap value-grid"><div><h2>Two shots. One lanyard. A whole BeltLine in costume.</h2><p>These are the benefits Bar Crawl USA currently publishes for this event. Check the official listing before you leave.</p></div><div class="included"><div>Entry to 6+ participating hotspots</div><div>Two complimentary shots</div><div>Published drink discounts</div><div>Event map and lanyard</div><div>Event photographer</div><div>$100 costume contest</div><div>No cover at participating BeltLine bars</div></div></div></section><section class="route-sec" id="route"><div class="wrap"><h2>BrewDog first. The trail decides the rest.</h2><p>Save the lineup, then check the official event page on crawl day for any venue update.</p><ol class="route"><li>BrewDog Krog District, registration and costume contest</li><li>Ranger Station</li><li>Eclipse di Luna</li><li>Guac y Margs</li><li>Chiringa</li><li>One Flew South</li><li>McCray's Tavern</li><li>Duke's Hideaway</li><li>Northern China Eatery</li><li>THChill Lounge</li></ol></div></section><section class="night"><div class="wrap split"><div><h2>Your Atlanta night works better with one simple plan.</h2></div><div><p>Start with the official event listing, confirm the registration point, and save the route before your group leaves home. Choose two places everybody wants to see, one place to reunite if the group splits, and the official after party when one is published. That leaves enough structure to keep the night moving without turning a bar crawl into a group project.</p><p>The published window is 6 PM to Midnight in Atlanta BeltLine Eastside Trail. Arrive early enough to check in without rushing, eat before the route gets loud, and keep the official ticket page handy for any same day change.</p></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><h2>Real Bar Crawl USA people. Real Atlanta energy.</h2><div class="gallery"><figure><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Atlanta-area-bar-crawl-usa-group.webp" alt="Atlanta friends posing together during a Bar Crawl USA event" loading="lazy" width="900" height="700"><figcaption>Atlanta friends posing together during a Bar Crawl USA event</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Boos-and-Booze-Halloween-Bar-Crawl-Partygoer.webp" alt="Costumed attendee at a Bar Crawl USA Boos and Booze Halloween event" loading="lazy" width="900" height="700"><figcaption>Costumed attendee at a Bar Crawl USA Boos and Booze Halloween event</figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section class="crew"><div class="wrap split"><div><h2>Wear the costume that can survive the Eastside Trail.</h2><p class="crew-note">Atlanta groups get the best night when one person owns check in, one person saves the official route, and everyone agrees on a final meetup point. Costumes should be comfortable enough for the Eastside Trail, and a light layer is a smart call for a late October night.</p></div><div class="plan"><h3>Make the smart plan before the first round.</h3><p>Bring a valid ID, keep the ticket confirmation easy to reach, and arrange a sober ride home before check in. Parking and transit information can change.</p><p><a href="https://beltline.org/parks-trails/eastside-trail/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Atlanta BeltLine Eastside Trail guide</a></p><p class="note">External planning resource. Bar Crawl USA does not control parking, transit, or street information.</p></div></div></section><section class="faq-sec"><div class="wrap split"><h2>Atlanta Halloween crawl questions, answered.</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>When is the Atlanta BeltLine Halloween bar crawl?</summary><p>The confirmed BeltLine edition runs Saturday, October 31, 2026 from 6 PM to midnight.</p></details><details><summary>Where does check in happen?</summary><p>BeltLine registration is at BrewDog Krog District. Use the official event page for the latest check in instructions.</p></details><details><summary>Is the route walkable?</summary><p>The published stops are organized around the BeltLine Eastside Trail. Comfortable shoes and a charged phone are recommended.</p></details><details><summary>What is included with a BeltLine ticket?</summary><p>The published package includes two complimentary shots, drink discounts, a map and lanyard, photographer coverage, costume contest access, and no cover at participating BeltLine bars.</p></details><details><summary>What are the 2026 Midtown details?</summary><p>A verified 2026 Midtown Halloween record is not public yet. This page will add those details only after Bar Crawl USA confirms them.</p></details></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><h2>Keep the night moving.</h2><nav class="related" aria-label="Related Bar Crawl USA pages"><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/bar-crawls-atlanta/">Atlanta bar crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Boos and Booze Halloween hub</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/event/atlanta-beltline-halloween-bar-crawl/">Official Atlanta event page</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/cleveland-halloween-bar-crawls-2026/">Cleveland Halloween crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/cincinnati-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">Cincinnati Halloween crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/columbia-sc-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">Columbia Halloween crawl guide</a></nav></div></section><section class="final"><div class="wrap"><h2>The BeltLine Has Costumes Now. Atlanta Has Plans. Ready?</h2><a class="btn" href="#tickets">Put Me on the BeltLine</a><p class="note">Review the official event listing for the latest operational details.</p></div></section>
