</style><style>.bcx .ticketing{background:var(--paper);border-top:1px solid var(--ink);border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink)}.bcx .ticketing-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr .9fr;gap:70px;align-items:center}.bcx .ticketing p{margin-bottom:0}.bcx .ticket-actions{display:grid;gap:18px}.bcx .ticket-choice{display:grid;gap:10px}.bcx .ticket-btn{width:100%;border:0;border-radius:0;cursor:pointer}.bcx .ticket-choice>a{font-weight:800;text-align:center}.bcx .ticket-btn:disabled{cursor:wait;opacity:.65}@media(max-width:820px){.bcx .ticketing-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:30px}}</style><main class="bcx campaign" style="--accent:#F2C94C" id="main-content"><header class="hero"><div class="hero-copy"><h1>Cleveland Halloween Bar Crawls 2026</h1><p class="lede">Cleveland Gets Two Saturdays. Choosing Just One Is Optional.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="#tickets">Show Me Both Cleveland Crawls</a><a class="btn alt" href="#route">See the route</a></div></div><div class="hero-media"><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/St-Paddys-Crawl-Cleveland.webp" alt="Friends celebrating together at a Cleveland Bar Crawl USA event" width="1200" height="900" fetchpriority="high"></div></header><div class="facts" aria-label="Event quick facts"><div class="fact"><span>Date</span><strong>October 24 + October 31</strong></div><div class="fact"><span>Published time</span><strong>4 PM to 10 PM</strong></div><div class="fact"><span>Neighborhood</span><strong>West Park and Lakewood</strong></div></div><section class="ticketing" id="tickets"><div class="wrap ticketing-grid"><div><h2>Tickets without the detour.</h2><p>Choose your event and complete the secure Eventbrite checkout without leaving this page. Use the event details link when you need the latest route or check in update.</p></div><div class="ticket-actions"><div class="ticket-choice"><button class="btn ticket-btn" id="eb-cleveland-halloween-bar-crawls-2026-1" type="button">Buy West Park tickets</button><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/event/cleveland-boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl-west-park-bars/">Review event details</a></div><div class="ticket-choice"><button class="btn ticket-btn" id="eb-cleveland-halloween-bar-crawls-2026-2" type="button">Buy Lakewood tickets</button><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/event/lakewood-boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Review event details</a></div></div></div></section><section class="story"><div class="wrap"><h2>West Park brings the tight neighborhood loop on October 24. Lakewood takes Halloween itself on October 31. Separate routes. Separate tickets. One city that clearly refused to keep Halloween to a single night.</h2><p>Cleveland area crawlers get a real choice in 2026. West Park takes over Saturday, October 24 with a compact neighborhood route and a return to West Park Station for the after party. Lakewood follows on Halloween, Saturday, October 31, with its own eight stop lineup. Pick the neighborhood that fits your crew, or make both weekends your Halloween plan.</p><p>The two editions should not be treated like duplicates. West Park is the tighter loop: register at West Park Station, move through five neighborhood bars, then come back for the official after party. Lakewood spreads the night across a longer Detroit Avenue area lineup, so your group should save the route and choose a reliable final meetup stop before the first round.</p><div class="edition-grid"><article><h3>West Park</h3><p>October 24 from 4 PM to 10 PM. Registration runs from 4 PM to 7 PM at West Park Station.</p><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/event/cleveland-boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl-west-park-bars/">Choose West Park</a></article><article><h3>Lakewood</h3><p>October 31 from 4 PM to 10 PM. Eight published Lakewood stops.</p><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/event/lakewood-boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Choose Lakewood</a></article></div></div></section><section class="value"><div class="wrap value-grid"><div><h2>Two neighborhoods. Two real routes. Zero copy and paste.</h2><p>These are the benefits Bar Crawl USA currently publishes for this event. Check the official listing before you leave.</p></div><div class="included"><div>Two complimentary shots</div><div>Published drink specials</div><div>Event map and lanyard</div><div>Official after party</div><div>Costume contest</div><div>Photographer on the Lakewood edition</div></div></div></section><section class="route-sec" id="route"><div class="wrap"><h2>West Park or Lakewood. Pick your Cleveland.</h2><p>Save the lineup, then check the official event page on crawl day for any venue update.</p><ol class="route"><li>WEST PARK: West Park Station, registration 4 to 7 PM</li><li>PJ McIntyre's</li><li>Smedley's Bar & Grill</li><li>Throwbacks</li><li>Backstage Bar</li><li>West Park Station, official after party</li><li>LAKEWOOD: Around the Corner</li><li>Halloween Corner Bar</li><li>Harry Buffalo</li><li>West End Tavern</li><li>Riverwood Cafe</li><li>Mercury Lounge</li><li>Lakewood Truck Park</li><li>Wine Dive</li></ol></div></section><section class="night"><div class="wrap split"><div><h2>Your Cleveland night works better with one simple plan.</h2></div><div><p>Start with the official event listing, confirm the registration point, and save the route before your group leaves home. Choose two places everybody wants to see, one place to reunite if the group splits, and the official after party when one is published. That leaves enough structure to keep the night moving without turning a bar crawl into a group project.</p><p>The published window is 4 PM to 10 PM in West Park and Lakewood. Arrive early enough to check in without rushing, eat before the route gets loud, and keep the official ticket page handy for any same day change.</p></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><h2>Real Bar Crawl USA people. Real Cleveland energy.</h2><div class="gallery"><figure><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Cleveland-BCU-1024x683.webp" alt="A lively group at a Bar Crawl USA event in Cleveland" loading="lazy" width="900" height="700"><figcaption>A lively group at a Bar Crawl USA event in Cleveland</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Boos-and-Booze-Halloween-Bar-Crawl-Partygoer.webp" alt="Costumed attendee at a Bar Crawl USA Boos and Booze Halloween event" loading="lazy" width="900" height="700"><figcaption>Costumed attendee at a Bar Crawl USA Boos and Booze Halloween event</figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section class="crew"><div class="wrap split"><div><h2>The group chat can argue. The dates cannot.</h2><p class="crew-note">West Park works well for groups that want an easy start and finish anchor. Lakewood suits crews who want more route variety. Either way, designate a check in lead, save both the event page and this guide, and decide whether your group is moving together or meeting at two planned stops.</p></div><div class="plan"><h3>Make the smart plan before the first round.</h3><p>Bring a valid ID, keep the ticket confirmation easy to reach, and arrange a sober ride home before check in. Parking and transit information can change.</p><p><a href="https://www.riderta.com/facilities/westpark" rel="noopener noreferrer">Plan around Cleveland transit and West Park Station</a></p><p class="note">External planning resource. Bar Crawl USA does not control parking, transit, or street information.</p></div></div></section><section class="faq-sec"><div class="wrap split"><h2>Cleveland Halloween crawl questions, answered.</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>What are the two Cleveland Halloween crawl dates?</summary><p>West Park runs October 24, 2026 and Lakewood runs October 31, 2026. Both published windows are 4 PM to 10 PM.</p></details><details><summary>Where is West Park registration?</summary><p>Registration is at West Park Station from 4 PM to 7 PM.</p></details><details><summary>Which 2026 Lakewood date is correct?</summary><p>The current event headline confirms Saturday, October 31. An older sentence in the source body contains a stale prior date and should not guide planning.</p></details><details><summary>Can I attend both editions?</summary><p>They take place on separate Saturdays, so you can plan for both if you purchase the appropriate ticket for each event.</p></details><details><summary>Do the two crawls use the same route?</summary><p>No. West Park and Lakewood have separate venue lineups and separate official event pages.</p></details></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><h2>Keep the night moving.</h2><nav class="related" aria-label="Related Bar Crawl USA pages"><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/cleveland-bar-crawls/">Cleveland bar crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Boos and Booze Halloween hub</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/event/cleveland-boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl-west-park-bars/">Official Cleveland event page</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/cincinnati-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">Cincinnati Halloween crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/columbia-sc-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">Columbia Halloween crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/greenville-sc-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">Greenville Halloween crawl guide</a></nav></div></section><section class="final"><div class="wrap"><h2>Cleveland Gets Two Saturdays. Choosing Just One Is Optional. Ready?</h2><a class="btn" href="#tickets">Show Me Both Cleveland Crawls</a><p class="note">Review the official event listing for the latest operational details.</p></div></section>
