</style><style>.bcx .ticketing{background:var(--paper);border-top:1px solid var(--ink);border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink)}.bcx .ticketing-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr .9fr;gap:70px;align-items:center}.bcx .ticketing p{margin-bottom:0}.bcx .ticket-actions{display:grid;gap:18px}.bcx .ticket-choice{display:grid;gap:10px}.bcx .ticket-btn{width:100%;border:0;border-radius:0;cursor:pointer}.bcx .ticket-choice>a{font-weight:800;text-align:center}.bcx .ticket-btn:disabled{cursor:wait;opacity:.65}@media(max-width:820px){.bcx .ticketing-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:30px}}</style><main class="bcx campaign" style="--accent:#E65A4F" id="main-content"><header class="hero"><div class="hero-copy"><h1>Cincinnati Halloween Bar Crawl 2026</h1><p class="lede">OTR Was Built for a Costume and a Wristband.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="#tickets">Take Me to the OTR Crawl</a><a class="btn alt" href="#route">See the route</a></div></div><div class="hero-media"><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Cincinnati-Bar-Crawl-USA-group.webp" alt="Friends at a Cincinnati Bar Crawl USA event" width="1200" height="900" fetchpriority="high"></div></header><div class="facts" aria-label="Event quick facts"><div class="fact"><span>Date</span><strong>Saturday, October 24</strong></div><div class="fact"><span>Published time</span><strong>4 PM to 10 PM</strong></div><div class="fact"><span>Neighborhood</span><strong>Over the Rhine</strong></div></div><section class="ticketing" id="tickets"><div class="wrap ticketing-grid"><div><h2>Tickets without the detour.</h2><p>Choose your event and complete the secure Eventbrite checkout without leaving this page. Use the event details link when you need the latest route or check in update.</p></div><div class="ticket-actions"><div class="ticket-choice"><button class="btn ticket-btn" id="eb-cincinnati-halloween-bar-crawl-2026-1" type="button">Buy Cincinnati tickets</button><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/event/cincinnati-boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Review event details</a></div></div></div></section><section class="story"><div class="wrap"><h2>Seven published stops turn Over the Rhine into one long Halloween decision. Start hungry, pick the bar your group refuses to miss, and let Rosedale settle the final round.</h2><p>Over the Rhine is built for a night that moves. Cincinnati's Boos & Booze crawl runs Saturday, October 24 from 4 PM to 10 PM, connecting seven published stops, two complimentary shots, drink specials, a costume contest, and an official Rosedale after party.</p><p>Check in early enough to get your map and lanyard before the route fills out, then let Main Street and the surrounding OTR blocks do the work. The route mixes cocktail rooms, a winery, dance friendly bars, and a final after party. If your crew has different priorities, pick Pilar or Revel as the first reunion point and Rosedale as the last.</p></div></section><section class="value"><div class="wrap value-grid"><div><h2>Two shots. Seven stops. One OTR Saturday.</h2><p>These are the benefits Bar Crawl USA currently publishes for this event. Check the official listing before you leave.</p></div><div class="included"><div>Access to 6+ OTR hotspots</div><div>Two complimentary shots</div><div>Published drink specials</div><div>Registration party and after party</div><div>Event photographer</div><div>Costume contest</div><div>Event map and lanyard</div></div></div></section><section class="route-sec" id="route"><div class="wrap"><h2>Main Street energy with a Rosedale finish.</h2><p>Save the lineup, then check the official event page on crawl day for any venue update.</p><ol class="route"><li>On the Rhine Eatery</li><li>Pilar</li><li>Revel Urban Winery</li><li>Bloom OTR</li><li>Nice Life</li><li>Japp's</li><li>Rosedale, official after party</li></ol></div></section><section class="night"><div class="wrap split"><div><h2>Your Cincinnati night works better with one simple plan.</h2></div><div><p>Start with the official event listing, confirm the registration point, and save the route before your group leaves home. Choose two places everybody wants to see, one place to reunite if the group splits, and the official after party when one is published. That leaves enough structure to keep the night moving without turning a bar crawl into a group project.</p><p>The published window is 4 PM to 10 PM in Over the Rhine. Arrive early enough to check in without rushing, eat before the route gets loud, and keep the official ticket page handy for any same day change.</p></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><h2>Real Bar Crawl USA people. Real Cincinnati energy.</h2><div class="gallery"><figure><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Bar-Crawl-USA-Cincinnati-Quad-1024x682.webp" alt="Four friends posing during a Cincinnati Bar Crawl USA event" loading="lazy" width="900" height="700"><figcaption>Four friends posing during a Cincinnati Bar Crawl USA event</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Boos-and-Booze-Halloween-Bar-Crawl-Partygoer.webp" alt="Costumed attendee at a Bar Crawl USA Boos and Booze Halloween event" loading="lazy" width="900" height="700"><figcaption>Costumed attendee at a Bar Crawl USA Boos and Booze Halloween event</figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section class="crew"><div class="wrap split"><div><h2>Cincinnati has strong costume opinions. Bring yours.</h2><p class="crew-note">Cincinnati costumes need to survive stairs, sidewalks, and a full OTR route. Build the group look around one unmistakable detail, keep hands free, and agree on a late night photo spot before everyone disappears into a different dance floor.</p></div><div class="plan"><h3>Make the smart plan before the first round.</h3><p>Bring a valid ID, keep the ticket confirmation easy to reach, and arrange a sober ride home before check in. Parking and transit information can change.</p><p><a href="https://www.cincinnati-oh.gov/parking/on-street-parking/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Check current City of Cincinnati on street parking information</a></p><p class="note">External planning resource. Bar Crawl USA does not control parking, transit, or street information.</p></div></div></section><section class="faq-sec"><div class="wrap split"><h2>Cincinnati Halloween crawl questions, answered.</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>When is the Cincinnati Halloween bar crawl?</summary><p>Saturday, October 24, 2026 from 4 PM to 10 PM.</p></details><details><summary>Which neighborhood is the crawl in?</summary><p>The published route is in Over the Rhine, commonly called OTR.</p></details><details><summary>What does a ticket include?</summary><p>Published inclusions are two complimentary shots, drink specials, photographer coverage, costume contest access, registration and after party access, plus a map and lanyard.</p></details><details><summary>Where is the after party?</summary><p>The published route identifies Rosedale as the official after party stop.</p></details><details><summary>Should I drive between stops?</summary><p>The route is designed around OTR. Plan to walk between nearby stops and arrange a sober ride home.</p></details></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><h2>Keep the night moving.</h2><nav class="related" aria-label="Related Bar Crawl USA pages"><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/cincinnati-bar-crawls/">Cincinnati bar crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Boos and Booze Halloween hub</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/event/cincinnati-boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Official Cincinnati event page</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/columbia-sc-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">Columbia Halloween crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/greenville-sc-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">Greenville Halloween crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/portland-me-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">Portland Halloween crawl guide</a></nav></div></section><section class="final"><div class="wrap"><h2>OTR Was Built for a Costume and a Wristband. Ready?</h2><a class="btn" href="#tickets">Take Me to the OTR Crawl</a><p class="note">Review the official event listing for the latest operational details.</p></div></section>
