</style><style>.bcx .ticketing{background:var(--paper);border-top:1px solid var(--ink);border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink)}.bcx .ticketing-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr .9fr;gap:70px;align-items:center}.bcx .ticketing p{margin-bottom:0}.bcx .ticket-actions{display:grid;gap:18px}.bcx .ticket-choice{display:grid;gap:10px}.bcx .ticket-btn{width:100%;border:0;border-radius:0;cursor:pointer}.bcx .ticket-choice>a{font-weight:800;text-align:center}.bcx .ticket-btn:disabled{cursor:wait;opacity:.65}@media(max-width:820px){.bcx .ticketing-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:30px}}</style><main class="bcx campaign" style="--accent:#EF8354" id="main-content"><header class="hero"><div class="hero-copy"><h1>Columbia SC Halloween Bar Crawl 2026</h1><p class="lede">The Vista Has Seen a Lot. This Night Still Wins.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="#tickets">Put Me in The Vista</a><a class="btn alt" href="#route">See the route</a></div></div><div class="hero-media"><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/columbia-bar-crawl-taco.webp" alt="Friends enjoying a themed Bar Crawl USA event in Columbia" width="1200" height="900" fetchpriority="high"></div></header><div class="facts" aria-label="Event quick facts"><div class="fact"><span>Date</span><strong>Saturday, October 24</strong></div><div class="fact"><span>Published time</span><strong>5 PM to 11 PM</strong></div><div class="fact"><span>Neighborhood</span><strong>The Vista</strong></div></div><section class="ticketing" id="tickets"><div class="wrap ticketing-grid"><div><h2>Tickets without the detour.</h2><p>Choose your event and complete the secure Eventbrite checkout without leaving this page. Use the event details link when you need the latest route or check in update.</p></div><div class="ticket-actions"><div class="ticket-choice"><button class="btn ticket-btn" id="eb-columbia-sc-halloween-bar-crawl-2026-1" type="button">Buy Columbia tickets</button><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/event/columbia-boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Review event details</a></div></div></div></section><section class="story"><div class="wrap"><h2>Tin Roof starts the conversation. Seven published stops keep it moving. Columbia gets six hours to prove that The Vista looks even better when everybody showed up in costume.</h2><p>The Vista turns into Columbia's Halloween circuit on Saturday, October 24. From 5 PM to 11 PM, Boos & Booze connects 6+ participating bars with two complimentary shots, published specials, a costume contest, map and lanyard, and an official after party.</p><p>The Vista keeps the route close enough to feel connected but varied enough that every stop has its own energy. Start with the official check in instructions, use Gervais Street as your orientation line, and choose whether your group wants live music, cocktails, or the after party to be the night's anchor.</p></div></section><section class="value"><div class="wrap value-grid"><div><h2>The Vista, two shots, and no weak group costume.</h2><p>These are the benefits Bar Crawl USA currently publishes for this event. Check the official listing before you leave.</p></div><div class="included"><div>Access to 6+ Vista bars</div><div>Two complimentary shots</div><div>Published drink specials</div><div>Official after party</div><div>Costume contest</div><div>Event map and lanyard</div></div></div></section><section class="route-sec" id="route"><div class="wrap"><h2>Seven names. One very loud district.</h2><p>Save the lineup, then check the official event page on crawl day for any venue update.</p><ol class="route"><li>Tin Roof</li><li>TakoSushi</li><li>Republic Biergarten & Kitchen</li><li>Pearlz Oyster Bar</li><li>Bailey's / Carolina Western Pub</li><li>Grill Marks</li><li>Vista Union</li></ol></div></section><section class="night"><div class="wrap split"><div><h2>Your Columbia night works better with one simple plan.</h2></div><div><p>Start with the official event listing, confirm the registration point, and save the route before your group leaves home. Choose two places everybody wants to see, one place to reunite if the group splits, and the official after party when one is published. That leaves enough structure to keep the night moving without turning a bar crawl into a group project.</p><p>The published window is 5 PM to 11 PM in The Vista. Arrive early enough to check in without rushing, eat before the route gets loud, and keep the official ticket page handy for any same day change.</p></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><h2>Real Bar Crawl USA people. Real Columbia energy.</h2><div class="gallery"><figure><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Columbia-taco-and-tequila-bar-crawl-usa-group-1024x683.webp" alt="A large group celebrating together at a Columbia Bar Crawl USA event" loading="lazy" width="900" height="700"><figcaption>A large group celebrating together at a Columbia Bar Crawl USA event</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Boos-and-Booze-Halloween-Bar-Crawl-Partygoer.webp" alt="Costumed attendee at a Bar Crawl USA Boos and Booze Halloween event" loading="lazy" width="900" height="700"><figcaption>Costumed attendee at a Bar Crawl USA Boos and Booze Halloween event</figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section class="crew"><div class="wrap split"><div><h2>Coordinate one detail. Let The Vista do the rest.</h2><p class="crew-note">The Vista is made for a strong group entrance. Coordinate one color, prop, or character universe, then keep the rest practical. A saved route guide and a named meetup bar will do more for the night than a group chat with fifty unread messages. Build in time for food before the costume contest and after party energy takes over.</p></div><div class="plan"><h3>Make the smart plan before the first round.</h3><p>Bring a valid ID, keep the ticket confirmation easy to reach, and arrange a sober ride home before check in. Parking and transit information can change.</p><p><a href="https://www.experiencecolumbiasc.com/listing/the-vista/15855/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore The Vista district</a></p><p class="note">External planning resource. Bar Crawl USA does not control parking, transit, or street information.</p></div></div></section><section class="faq-sec"><div class="wrap split"><h2>Columbia Halloween crawl questions, answered.</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>When is Columbia's Boos & Booze crawl?</summary><p>Saturday, October 24, 2026 from 5 PM to 11 PM.</p></details><details><summary>Where does it take place?</summary><p>The published route is centered in The Vista in Columbia, South Carolina.</p></details><details><summary>How many bars are included?</summary><p>The event promotes 6+ participating bars and currently names seven route stops.</p></details><details><summary>What comes with a ticket?</summary><p>Two complimentary shots, published specials, costume contest access, an official after party, and an event map and lanyard are listed.</p></details><details><summary>Is the route finalized?</summary><p>Use the official event page on crawl day for any operational updates or venue changes.</p></details></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><h2>Keep the night moving.</h2><nav class="related" aria-label="Related Bar Crawl USA pages"><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/columbia-bar-crawls/">Columbia bar crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Boos and Booze Halloween hub</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/event/columbia-boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Official Columbia event page</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/greenville-sc-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">Greenville Halloween crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/portland-me-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">Portland Halloween crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/st-pete-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">St. Pete Halloween crawl guide</a></nav></div></section><section class="final"><div class="wrap"><h2>The Vista Has Seen a Lot. This Night Still Wins. Ready?</h2><a class="btn" href="#tickets">Put Me in The Vista</a><p class="note">Review the official event listing for the latest operational details.</p></div></section>
