</style><style>.bcx .ticketing{background:var(--paper);border-top:1px solid var(--ink);border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink)}.bcx .ticketing-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr .9fr;gap:70px;align-items:center}.bcx .ticketing p{margin-bottom:0}.bcx .ticket-actions{display:grid;gap:18px}.bcx .ticket-choice{display:grid;gap:10px}.bcx .ticket-btn{width:100%;border:0;border-radius:0;cursor:pointer}.bcx .ticket-choice>a{font-weight:800;text-align:center}.bcx .ticket-btn:disabled{cursor:wait;opacity:.65}@media(max-width:820px){.bcx .ticketing-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:30px}}</style><main class="bcx campaign" style="--accent:#7ED957" id="main-content"><header class="hero"><div class="hero-copy"><h1>Greenville SC Halloween Bar Crawl 2026</h1><p class="lede">Falls Park Will Still Be There Sunday. Halloween Is Saturday.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="#tickets">Take Me Downtown</a><a class="btn alt" href="#route">See the route</a></div></div><div class="hero-media"><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Greenville-St-Paddy.webp" alt="Friends at a themed Bar Crawl USA event in Greenville" width="1200" height="900" fetchpriority="high"></div></header><div class="facts" aria-label="Event quick facts"><div class="fact"><span>Date</span><strong>Saturday, October 24</strong></div><div class="fact"><span>Published time</span><strong>5 PM to 11 PM</strong></div><div class="fact"><span>Neighborhood</span><strong>Downtown Greenville</strong></div></div><section class="ticketing" id="tickets"><div class="wrap ticketing-grid"><div><h2>Tickets without the detour.</h2><p>Choose your event and complete the secure Eventbrite checkout without leaving this page. Use the event details link when you need the latest route or check in update.</p></div><div class="ticket-actions"><div class="ticket-choice"><button class="btn ticket-btn" id="eb-greenville-sc-halloween-bar-crawl-2026-1" type="button">Buy Greenville tickets</button><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/event/greenville-boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Review event details</a></div></div></div></section><section class="story"><div class="wrap"><h2>Downtown Greenville gets eight published stops, two complimentary shots, and a route with enough personality to keep Main Street interesting from the first check in through the final round.</h2><p>Downtown Greenville gets a full Halloween route on Saturday, October 24. The 5 PM to 11 PM crawl links a published lineup of bars around Main Street with two complimentary shots, drink specials, a costume contest, map and lanyard, and the official after party.</p><p>Greenville's route stretches across different styles of night out: dueling pianos, taverns, cocktail bars, and late night dance energy. Do not try to force every stop. Pick one early anchor, one mid route wildcard, and one finale so your group can actually enjoy the places it chooses.</p></div></section><section class="value"><div class="wrap value-grid"><div><h2>Main Street, two shots, and a costume worth photographing.</h2><p>These are the benefits Bar Crawl USA currently publishes for this event. Check the official listing before you leave.</p></div><div class="included"><div>Published downtown venue lineup</div><div>Two complimentary shots</div><div>Published drink specials</div><div>Official after party</div><div>Costume contest</div><div>Event map and lanyard</div></div></div></section><section class="route-sec" id="route"><div class="wrap"><h2>Pick three must stops. Let downtown surprise you.</h2><p>Save the lineup, then check the official event page on crawl day for any venue update.</p><ol class="route"><li>Carolina Ale House</li><li>TakoSushi</li><li>Jack n' Diane's Dueling Pianos</li><li>DT's Tavern</li><li>Lost & Found</li><li>Sharkey's Pub</li><li>Reys</li><li>Abanico</li></ol></div></section><section class="night"><div class="wrap split"><div><h2>Your Greenville night works better with one simple plan.</h2></div><div><p>Start with the official event listing, confirm the registration point, and save the route before your group leaves home. Choose two places everybody wants to see, one place to reunite if the group splits, and the official after party when one is published. That leaves enough structure to keep the night moving without turning a bar crawl into a group project.</p><p>The published window is 5 PM to 11 PM in Downtown Greenville. Arrive early enough to check in without rushing, eat before the route gets loud, and keep the official ticket page handy for any same day change.</p></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><h2>Real Bar Crawl USA people. Real Greenville energy.</h2><div class="gallery"><figure><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Greenville-group-ugly-sweater-bar-crawl-usa-1024x683.webp" alt="A Greenville group posing together during a Bar Crawl USA event" loading="lazy" width="900" height="700"><figcaption>A Greenville group posing together during a Bar Crawl USA event</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Boos-and-Booze-Halloween-Bar-Crawl-Partygoer.webp" alt="Costumed attendee at a Bar Crawl USA Boos and Booze Halloween event" loading="lazy" width="900" height="700"><figcaption>Costumed attendee at a Bar Crawl USA Boos and Booze Halloween event</figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section class="crew"><div class="wrap split"><div><h2>The best Greenville costume can still walk Main Street.</h2><p class="crew-note">Greenville is a dress up city on Halloween weekend, so commit to the costume. Just keep the shoes walkable and the props compact. Groups should choose a Main Street meetup point that is easy to describe without dropping a map pin. A clear mid route check in will keep a long downtown lineup from turning into three separate nights.</p></div><div class="plan"><h3>Make the smart plan before the first round.</h3><p>Bring a valid ID, keep the ticket confirmation easy to reach, and arrange a sober ride home before check in. Parking and transit information can change.</p><p><a href="https://www.greenvillesc.gov/parking" rel="noopener noreferrer">Plan downtown parking with the City of Greenville</a></p><p class="note">External planning resource. Bar Crawl USA does not control parking, transit, or street information.</p></div></div></section><section class="faq-sec"><div class="wrap split"><h2>Greenville Halloween crawl questions, answered.</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>When is the Greenville Halloween bar crawl?</summary><p>Saturday, October 24, 2026 from 5 PM to 11 PM.</p></details><details><summary>Where is the route?</summary><p>The published venues are in downtown Greenville, South Carolina.</p></details><details><summary>How many stops are listed?</summary><p>The current route names eight venues. The event source also promotes a multi bar downtown crawl.</p></details><details><summary>What is included?</summary><p>Two complimentary shots, published drink specials, the costume contest, after party access, and an event map and lanyard are listed.</p></details><details><summary>Where should I check for changes?</summary><p>Use the official Bar Crawl USA event page for the latest check in, venue, and ticket information.</p></details></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><h2>Keep the night moving.</h2><nav class="related" aria-label="Related Bar Crawl USA pages"><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/greenville-bar-crawls/">Greenville bar crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Boos and Booze Halloween hub</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/event/greenville-boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Official Greenville event page</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/portland-me-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">Portland Halloween crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/st-pete-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">St. Pete Halloween crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/macon-ga-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/