</style><style>.bcx .ticketing{background:var(--paper);border-top:1px solid var(--ink);border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink)}.bcx .ticketing-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr .9fr;gap:70px;align-items:center}.bcx .ticketing p{margin-bottom:0}.bcx .ticket-actions{display:grid;gap:18px}.bcx .ticket-choice{display:grid;gap:10px}.bcx .ticket-btn{width:100%;border:0;border-radius:0;cursor:pointer}.bcx .ticket-choice>a{font-weight:800;text-align:center}.bcx .ticket-btn:disabled{cursor:wait;opacity:.65}@media(max-width:820px){.bcx .ticketing-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:30px}}</style><main class="bcx portland" style="--accent:#46B5D1" id="main-content"><header class="hero"><div class="hero-copy"><h1>Portland ME Halloween Bar Crawl 2026</h1><p class="lede">The Old Port Keeps the Best Stories After Dark.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="#tickets">Claim My Old Port Night</a><a class="btn alt" href="#route">See the route</a></div></div><div class="hero-media"><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/482016788_671628605396491_6648303472999453234_n-e1781033647367.jpg" alt="Friends in creative costumes at the Portland Maine Halloween bar crawl" width="1200" height="900" fetchpriority="high"></div></header><div class="facts" aria-label="Event quick facts"><div class="fact"><span>Date</span><strong>Saturday, October 24</strong></div><div class="fact"><span>Published time</span><strong>Crawl 4 PM to 10 PM</strong></div><div class="fact"><span>Neighborhood</span><strong>Portland Old Port</strong></div></div><section class="ticketing" id="tickets"><div class="wrap ticketing-grid"><div><h2>Tickets without the detour.</h2><p>Choose your event and complete the secure Eventbrite checkout without leaving this page. Use the event details link when you need the latest route or check in update.</p></div><div class="ticket-actions"><div class="ticket-choice"><button class="btn ticket-btn" id="eb-portland-me-halloween-bar-crawl-2026-1" type="button">Buy Portland tickets</button><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/event/portland-boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Review event details</a></div></div></div></section><section class="story"><div class="wrap"><h2>Fore Play opens the route. The Porthole closes it at 11. Everything between them is Portland proving that one of America's best food cities also knows exactly what to do with Halloween.</h2><p>Portland's Old Port crawl runs 4 PM to 10 PM on Saturday, October 24, then keeps the official celebration going at the Porthole after party at 11 PM. The route covers nine published stops with two complimentary shots, drink specials, photographer coverage, a $100 costume contest, and a map and lanyard.</p><p>The Old Port's brick sidewalks and compact blocks make this a classic walking crawl, but the waterfront air can feel colder after dark. Check in at Fore Play, build your route around two or three must hit pubs, and treat the 11 PM Porthole after party as a separate finale rather than part of the 4 PM to 10 PM crawl window.</p></div></section><section class="route-sec" id="route"><div class="wrap"><h2>Nine Old Port stops, printed in the order you need.</h2><p>Save the lineup, then check the official event page on crawl day for any venue update.</p><ol class="route"><li>Fore Play Sports Bar, registration</li><li>Glass Lounge</li><li>Tomaso's Pizza & Bar</li><li>Three Dollar Deweys</li><li>Bonfire Country Bar</li><li>Gritty McDuff's</li><li>Rosie's Pub</li><li>Andy's Old Port Pub</li><li>The Porthole, after party at 11 PM</li></ol></div></section><section class="night"><div class="wrap split"><div><h2>Your Portland night works better with one simple plan.</h2></div><div><p>Start with the official event listing, confirm the registration point, and save the route before your group leaves home. Choose two places everybody wants to see, one place to reunite if the group splits, and the official after party when one is published. That leaves enough structure to keep the night moving without turning a bar crawl into a group project.</p><p>The published window is Crawl 4 PM to 10 PM in Portland Old Port. Arrive early enough to check in without rushing, eat before the route gets loud, and keep the official ticket page handy for any same day change.</p></div></div></section><section class="value"><div class="wrap value-grid"><div><h2>The crawl ends at 10. The Porthole gets the next hour.</h2><p>These are the benefits Bar Crawl USA currently publishes for this event. Check the official listing before you leave.</p></div><div class="included"><div>Old Port venue route</div><div>Two complimentary shots</div><div>Published drink specials</div><div>Event photographer</div><div>$100 costume contest</div><div>Event map and lanyard</div><div>Separate 11 PM Porthole after party</div></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><h2>Real Bar Crawl USA people. Real Portland energy.</h2><div class="gallery"><figure><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Portland-Bar-Crawl-USA-group.webp" alt="Friends at a Portland Maine Bar Crawl USA event" loading="lazy" width="900" height="700"><figcaption>Friends at a Portland Maine Bar Crawl USA event</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Portland-Bar-Crawl-Cocktails.webp" alt="Cocktails served during a Portland Bar Crawl USA event" loading="lazy" width="900" height="700"><figcaption>Cocktails served during a Portland Bar Crawl USA event</figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section class="faq-sec"><div class="wrap split"><h2>Portland Halloween crawl questions, answered.</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>When is the Portland Maine Halloween bar crawl?</summary><p>The published crawl window is Saturday, October 24, 2026 from 4 PM to 10 PM.</p></details><details><summary>Why does the route mention 11 PM?</summary><p>The Porthole after party begins at 11 PM and is presented separately from the 4 PM to 10 PM crawl window.</p></details><details><summary>Where is registration?</summary><p>The published route identifies Fore Play Sports Bar as registration.</p></details><details><summary>What is included?</summary><p>Two complimentary shots, drink specials, photographer coverage, a $100 costume contest, an event map and lanyard, plus the official after party are listed.</p></details><details><summary>Is this Portland, Oregon?</summary><p>No. This event takes place in Portland, Maine, in the Old Port.</p></details></div></div></section><section class="crew"><div class="wrap split"><div><h2>Maine weather gets a vote. Give your costume a layer.</h2><p class="crew-note">Portland costumes should work with a jacket, not fight one. Build layers into the look and wear shoes that can handle brick streets. If the crew splits, reunite at the Porthole rather than chasing each other through every stop.</p></div><div class="plan"><h3>Make the smart plan before the first round.</h3><p>Bring a valid ID, keep the ticket confirmation easy to reach, and arrange a sober ride home before check in. Parking and transit information can change.</p><p><a href="https://portlandmaine.com/getting-around-portland/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Review Downtown Portland parking options</a></p><p class="note">External planning resource. Bar Crawl USA does not control parking, transit, or street information.</p></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><h2>Keep the night moving.</h2><nav class="related" aria-label="Related Bar Crawl USA pages"><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/portland-bar-crawls/">Portland bar crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Boos and Booze Halloween hub</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/event/portland-boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Official Portland event page</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/st-pete-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">St. Pete Halloween crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/macon-ga-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">Macon Halloween crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/roswell-ga-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">Roswell Halloween crawl guide</a></nav></div></section><section class="final"><div class="wrap"><h2>The Old Port Keeps the Best Stories After Dark. Ready?</h2><a class="btn" href="#tickets">Claim My Old Port Night</a><p class="note">Review the official event listing for the latest operational details.</p></div></section>
