</style><style>.bcx .ticketing{background:var(--paper);border-top:1px solid var(--ink);border-bottom:1px solid var(--ink)}.bcx .ticketing-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr .9fr;gap:70px;align-items:center}.bcx .ticketing p{margin-bottom:0}.bcx .ticket-actions{display:grid;gap:18px}.bcx .ticket-choice{display:grid;gap:10px}.bcx .ticket-btn{width:100%;border:0;border-radius:0;cursor:pointer}.bcx .ticket-choice>a{font-weight:800;text-align:center}.bcx .ticket-btn:disabled{cursor:wait;opacity:.65}@media(max-width:820px){.bcx .ticketing-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:30px}}</style><main class="bcx stpete" style="--accent:#F7C548" id="main-content"><header class="hero"><div class="hero-copy"><h1>St. Pete Halloween Bar Crawl 2026</h1><p class="lede">The Beach Gets Tomorrow. Central Avenue Gets Tonight.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn" href="#tickets">Put Me on Central Avenue</a><a class="btn alt" href="#route">See the route</a></div></div><div class="hero-media"><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/484108758_671627228729962_6616937303060195282_n-1-e1754326298825.jpg" alt="Costumed friends at a Bar Crawl USA Halloween event" width="1200" height="900" fetchpriority="high"></div></header><div class="facts" aria-label="Event quick facts"><div class="fact"><span>Date</span><strong>Saturday, October 24</strong></div><div class="fact"><span>Published time</span><strong>4 PM to 10 PM</strong></div><div class="fact"><span>Neighborhood</span><strong>Downtown St. Petersburg</strong></div></div><section class="ticketing" id="tickets"><div class="wrap ticketing-grid"><div><h2>Tickets without the detour.</h2><p>Choose your event and complete the secure Eventbrite checkout without leaving this page. Use the event details link when you need the latest route or check in update.</p></div><div class="ticket-actions"><div class="ticket-choice"><button class="btn ticket-btn" id="eb-st-pete-halloween-bar-crawl-2026-1" type="button">Buy St. Pete tickets</button><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/event/st-pete-boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Review event details</a></div></div></div></section><section class="value"><div class="wrap value-grid"><div><h2>Sunset first. Seven plus bars next. Thirsty First last.</h2><p>These are the benefits Bar Crawl USA currently publishes for this event. Check the official listing before you leave.</p></div><div class="included"><div>Access to 7+ downtown bars</div><div>Two complimentary shots</div><div>Published drink specials</div><div>Event photographer</div><div>Costume contest</div><div>Event map and lanyard</div><div>Official Thirsty First after party</div></div></div></section><section class="story"><div class="wrap"><h2>Dublin Drop starts the check in. Thirsty First owns the after party. Between them, Downtown St. Petersburg gets thirteen named stops and one very good reason to skip the usual Saturday.</h2><p>Downtown St. Petersburg packs a long venue lineup into one Saturday. Boos & Booze runs October 24 from 4 PM to 10 PM with 7+ participating bars, two complimentary shots, published drink specials, photographer coverage, costume contest access, map and lanyard, and a Thirsty First after party.</p><p>Central Avenue and the surrounding downtown blocks reward groups that plan lightly. Register at Dublin Drop, save the full list, then choose the energy you want: country bar, tequila stop, neighborhood pub, or dance heavy finale. The route has more named venues than most crews will realistically visit, and that is a feature, not a challenge.</p></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><h2>Real Bar Crawl USA people. Real St. Pete energy.</h2><div class="gallery"><figure><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/St-Pete-bar-crawl-group-BBQ_Beer_Bourbon_Crawl_2020_013.webp" alt="A group enjoying a Bar Crawl USA event in St. Pete" loading="lazy" width="900" height="700"><figcaption>A group enjoying a Bar Crawl USA event in St. Pete</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="https://barcrawlusa.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/Ugly-Sweater-group-St-Pete-2023_104.webp" alt="Friends in themed outfits at a St. Pete Bar Crawl USA event" loading="lazy" width="900" height="700"><figcaption>Friends in themed outfits at a St. Pete Bar Crawl USA event</figcaption></figure></div></div></section><section class="route-sec" id="route"><div class="wrap"><h2>A Central Avenue night with a clear beginning and ending.</h2><p>Save the lineup, then check the official event page on crawl day for any venue update.</p><ol class="route"><li>Dublin Drop, registration</li><li>Who's on First</li><li>Dublin</li><li>One Night Stand</li><li>Tequila Daisy</li><li>Pelican Pub</li><li>The Landing</li><li>Five Bucks Drinkery</li><li>Pour Judgement</li><li>Crafty Squirrel</li><li>Henley</li><li>Where's Jubes</li><li>Thirsty First, official after party</li></ol></div></section><section class="night"><div class="wrap split"><div><h2>Your St. Pete night works better with one simple plan.</h2></div><div><p>Start with the official event listing, confirm the registration point, and save the route before your group leaves home. Choose two places everybody wants to see, one place to reunite if the group splits, and the official after party when one is published. That leaves enough structure to keep the night moving without turning a bar crawl into a group project.</p><p>The published window is 4 PM to 10 PM in Downtown St. Petersburg. Arrive early enough to check in without rushing, eat before the route gets loud, and keep the official ticket page handy for any same day change.</p></div></div></section><section class="crew"><div class="wrap split"><div><h2>Sunscreen can clock out. Your costume cannot.</h2><p class="crew-note">St. Pete heat and late October humidity can still punish a heavy costume. Choose breathable layers, secure props, and comfortable shoes. Set one Central Avenue meetup point and one after party meetup so the night can flex without losing people.</p></div><div class="plan"><h3>Make the smart plan before the first round.</h3><p>Bring a valid ID, keep the ticket confirmation easy to reach, and arrange a sober ride home before check in. Parking and transit information can change.</p><p><a href="https://www.stpete.org/Residents/parking_transportation/Printable_DTStPete.pdf" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open the Downtown St. Petersburg parking guide</a></p><p class="note">External planning resource. Bar Crawl USA does not control parking, transit, or street information.</p></div></div></section><section class="faq-sec"><div class="wrap split"><h2>St. Pete Halloween crawl questions, answered.</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>When is the St. Pete Halloween bar crawl?</summary><p>Saturday, October 24, 2026 from 4 PM to 10 PM.</p></details><details><summary>Where is registration?</summary><p>The published route identifies Dublin Drop as the registration stop.</p></details><details><summary>How many venues are on the route?</summary><p>The current route names thirteen stops, including registration and the Thirsty First after party.</p></details><details><summary>What is included?</summary><p>Two complimentary shots, published specials, photographer coverage, costume contest access, an event map and lanyard, and the official after party are listed.</p></details><details><summary>Is St. Pete the same as St. Petersburg for this event?</summary><p>Yes. The route is in Downtown St. Petersburg, Florida, and Bar Crawl USA also uses the familiar St. Pete name.</p></details></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><h2>Keep the night moving.</h2><nav class="related" aria-label="Related Bar Crawl USA pages"><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/st-pete-bar-crawls/">St. Pete bar crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Boos and Booze Halloween hub</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/event/st-pete-boos-booze-halloween-bar-crawl/">Official St. Pete event page</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/macon-ga-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">Macon Halloween crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/roswell-ga-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">Roswell Halloween crawl guide</a><a href="https://barcrawlusa.com/sarasota-halloween-bar-crawl-2026/">Sarasota Halloween crawl guide</a></nav></div></section><section class="final"><div class="wrap"><h2>The Beach Gets Tomorrow. Central Avenue Gets Tonight. Ready?</h2><a class="btn" href="#tickets">Put Me on Central Avenue</a><p class="note">Review the official event listing for the latest operational details.</p></div></section>
